  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Dimensional formula for Torque</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#964;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now the percentage error in torque can be calculated by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#964;</mi><mo>%</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
